<title>RUSSIA: RUSSIAN 1996 GOLD OUTPUT FELL 7.0 PCT FROM 1995.</title>
<headline>RUSSIAN 1996 GOLD OUTPUT FELL 7.0 PCT FROM 1995.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian gold production fell 7.0 percent in 1996 from 1995, the State Statistics Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>It released no outright production figures, but gave the following percentage changes for non-ferrous metals and gold output.</p>
<p>Nickel output down 3.0 percent</p>
<p>Cobalt output down 6.0 percent</p>
<p>Aluminium output up 3.0 percent</p>
<p>Refined copper output up 7.0 percent</p>
</text>
